# Copy to .env and fill in what you want. Everything is optional.
# Restart the app after changing it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- AI (optional)
# Writes research briefs and reads plain-language screener questions. Without it, or whenever a call fails or
# times out, the app uses its rule-based brief and keyword parser instead.
#
# AI_PROVIDER   anthropic | openai_compatible | none
# AI_BASE_URL   the API's address (openai_compatible: everything before /chat/completions)
# AI_MODEL      the model name as the provider spells it
# AI_API_KEY    leave empty for local servers like Ollama and LM Studio. Several keys, separated by commas, take
#               turns: one that reaches a rate limit rests (as long as the provider says) and the next carries on
# AI_TIMEOUT    seconds to wait; default 180 for a server on this computer or network, 90 otherwise
# AI_THINKING   for models that reason before answering (gemma4, qwen3, gpt-oss, deepseek-r1...):
#               off    answer straight away: much faster. Sent as reasoning_effort "none", which Ollama understands.
#               on     let it think, with six times the usual room so the reasoning can't use up the reply.
#               low / medium / high   how hard to think, for models with effort levels (gpt-oss on Groq).
#               Leave it unset for models that don't reason, or providers that reject reasoning_effort.
#
# Pick one block and uncomment it.

# Ollama, running on this computer (https://ollama.com; `ollama pull gemma4:e4b` first)
# AI_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# AI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# AI_MODEL=gemma4:e4b
# AI_THINKING=off

# LM Studio, with its local server started (the model name is shown in LM Studio)
# AI_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# AI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
# AI_MODEL=qwen2.5-7b-instruct

# OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai/keys)
# AI_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# AI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# AI_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct
# AI_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# Groq (https://console.groq.com/keys). Check the model list there: Groq changes it from time to time.
# AI_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# AI_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# AI_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# AI_API_KEY=gsk_...
# AI_THINKING=on
# (llama-3.3-70b-versatile also works; it doesn't reason, so leave AI_THINKING out for it.)

# Anthropic (https://console.anthropic.com). An older .env with only ANTHROPIC_API_KEY also still works.
# AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
# AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# AI_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- web search for Ask AI
# With a Tavily key, Ask searches the web through Tavily: each result comes with its link, and it works with any
# provider above. Free plan: 1,000 searches a month (https://tavily.com).
# Without one, a gpt-oss model on Groq uses Groq's own browser search instead (no links to the pages it read, and
# what it reads counts toward your Groq allowance). Anything else: no web search.
# WEB_SEARCH    auto (the default) | tavily | groq | off
# Several keys, separated by commas, are used in turn: one that reaches its limit hands over to the next.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- data and alerts
# 1 = synthetic offline data (no internet needed) - useful for trying the UI
CLEARYIELD_DEMO=0

# How often alerts are checked while the app runs
ALERT_CHECK_MINUTES=15

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- email alerts (optional)
# Emails triggered alerts through your own mail account. Turn it on and choose the address in Settings, Email alerts;
# "Send test email" there checks this setup. Alerts are only checked while the app is running.
#
# SMTP_HOST      your provider's outgoing mail server
# SMTP_PORT      587 (the default, STARTTLS) or 465 (SSL)
# SMTP_USER      the account's user name, usually its full address
# SMTP_PASSWORD  for Gmail and Outlook.com an app password, not your normal one. Gmail: turn on 2-Step Verification,
#                then Google Account > Security > App passwords
# SMTP_FROM      the address emails come from; SMTP_USER if left out
# SMTP_SECURITY  starttls | ssl | none; worked out from the port if left out
#
# Gmail
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com
# (the app password: the 16 letters Google shows, without the spaces)
# SMTP_PASSWORD=abcdefghijklmnop
#
# Outlook.com / Hotmail: smtp-mail.outlook.com, port 587. Yahoo Mail: smtp.mail.yahoo.com, port 465.
